from s5_lib import *
# ---- 1 Secure access with Microsoft Entra ID
C(1,"PIM: eligible vs active assignment?","**Eligible:** the user must **activate** the role when needed (can require MFA, justification, approval, a ticket) and it expires after a set time. **Active:** the role is on without activation. PIM gives **just-in-time, time-bound, audited** privileged access.")
C(1,"What can PIM manage?","**Microsoft Entra roles**, **Azure resource roles** (Owner, Contributor and others at any scope) and **PIM for Groups** (just-in-time membership or ownership). Pair it with **access reviews** to remove assignments nobody needs.")
C(1,"Conditional Access: the building blocks?","**Assignments** (users or workload/agent identities, target resources, conditions such as location, device platform, client app, sign-in risk, user risk) and **access controls**: **grant** (block, require MFA, authentication strength, compliant device) and **session** (sign-in frequency, app-enforced restrictions).")
C(1,"How do you roll out a Conditional Access policy safely?","Start in **report-only** mode and check the sign-in logs. **Exclude emergency (break-glass) accounts.** Use the **What If** tool to test who a policy hits.")
C(1,"Phishing-resistant authentication methods?","**Passkeys (FIDO2)**, **Windows Hello for Business** and **certificate-based authentication**. Enforce them with a Conditional Access **authentication strength**. SMS and voice are the weakest methods.")
C(1,"App registration vs enterprise application?","**App registration:** the global **application object**, where you define the app (redirect URIs, API permissions, secrets or certificates). **Enterprise application:** the **service principal**, the app's local identity in a tenant, where you control sign-in, assignment and consent.")
C(1,"Delegated vs application permissions?","**Delegated:** the app acts **as the signed-in user**, limited by what that user can do. **Application:** the app acts **as itself** with no user, and always needs **admin consent**.")
C(1,"Consent settings worth knowing?","Limit **user consent** to verified publishers and low-risk permissions (or turn it off), and turn on the **admin consent workflow** so users can request approval. Review and revoke grants under Enterprise applications → Permissions.")
C(1,"System-assigned vs user-assigned managed identity?","**System-assigned:** tied to one resource and deleted with it. **User-assigned:** a standalone resource you can attach to **many** resources. Both remove secrets from code; grant them Azure RBAC roles.")
Q(1,"Admins must hold the Security Administrator role only when they need it, after approval, for at most four hours. What should you configure?","An eligible assignment in Privileged Identity Management with approval required",["An active permanent assignment","A Conditional Access policy that blocks the role","A dynamic group with the role"],"Eligible PIM assignments are activated just in time, with approval and a time limit.")
Q(1,"You are about to enforce MFA for all users with Conditional Access. What should you do first to avoid locking out the tenant?","Exclude the emergency access accounts and run the policy in report-only mode",["Assign the policy to Global Administrators only","Disable security defaults and all other policies","Delete legacy authentication protocols from the tenant"],"Break-glass accounts are excluded, and report-only shows the impact before enforcement.")
Q(1,"A daemon service with no signed-in user must read all users' mailboxes through Microsoft Graph. Which permission type is needed?","Application permissions with admin consent",["Delegated permissions with user consent","Delegated permissions with admin consent","No permissions; daemons are trusted"],"With no user present the app acts as itself, which needs application permissions and admin consent.")
Q(1,"Which TWO authentication methods are phishing-resistant?",["Passkey (FIDO2)","Windows Hello for Business"],["SMS one-time code","Voice call"],"FIDO2 passkeys and Windows Hello for Business are bound to the device and origin. SMS and voice can be intercepted or phished.")
YN(1,["An application permission can be granted by any user through user consent.","A user-assigned managed identity can be attached to more than one Azure resource.","PIM can require MFA when a user activates a role."],[0,1,1],"Application permissions always need admin consent. User-assigned identities are shareable. PIM activation settings include MFA.")
M(1,"Match each need to the Entra feature.",[("Just-in-time admin roles","Privileged Identity Management"),("Require a compliant device for an app","Conditional Access"),("Let users ask an admin to approve an app","Admin consent workflow"),("VM reads Key Vault with no stored secret","Managed identity")],"One feature per job.")
Q(1,"Where do you restrict which users may sign in to a SaaS app that is integrated with Entra ID?","On the enterprise application (service principal): require assignment and assign users",["On the app registration's redirect URIs","In the app's API permissions","In the tenant's custom domain settings"],"User assignment and sign-in controls live on the enterprise application.")
Q(1,"Users keep approving risky third-party apps. You want them to request approval instead of granting consent themselves. What should you configure?","Restrict user consent and enable the admin consent workflow",["Grant tenant-wide admin consent to all apps","Make all users Cloud Application Administrators","Disable all enterprise applications"],"Limiting user consent stops the risky grants, and the workflow routes requests to reviewers.")
D(1,"Eligible assignment","Active assignment","Must be activated before the role works.",0,"Eligible roles are activated just in time.")
D(1,"App registration","Enterprise application","Where you require user assignment for sign-in.",1,"The service principal controls access in your tenant.")
D(1,"Delegated permission","Application permission","Works without a signed-in user and always needs admin consent.",1,"Application permissions are app-only.")
D(1,"System-assigned identity","User-assigned identity","Deleted automatically when its resource is deleted.",0,"System-assigned identities share the resource's lifecycle.")
# ---- 2 Azure Key Vault
C(2,"What does Key Vault store, and which tiers exist?","**Secrets** (passwords, connection strings), **keys** (cryptographic keys) and **certificates**. **Standard** protects keys with software; **Premium** adds **HSM-protected keys**. **Managed HSM** is a separate single-tenant HSM service.")
C(2,"Key Vault access models?","**Azure RBAC** (recommended): roles at vault, or even single-object scope. **Vault access policies** (legacy): per-vault permission lists. The **management plane** (create the vault, settings) and **data plane** (read secrets, use keys) are authorized separately.")
C(2,"Key Vault data-plane RBAC roles to recognize?","**Key Vault Administrator** (all data-plane), **Secrets Officer** (manage secrets), **Secrets User** (read secret values), **Crypto Officer** (manage keys), **Crypto User** (use keys), **Certificates Officer**, **Reader** (metadata only), **Purge Operator**.")
C(2,"Soft delete in Key Vault?","On by default and **cannot be turned off**. Deleted vaults and objects stay recoverable for **7 to 90 days** (default 90); the period is set at creation and **cannot be changed**. A deleted name cannot be reused until it is purged or expires.")
C(2,"Purge protection?","Optional, **off by default**. When on, **nobody, not even Microsoft**, can purge a deleted vault or object until the retention period ends, and it **cannot be disabled**. Required by services that use customer-managed keys.")
C(2,"Key Vault network controls?","Firewall: **disable public access** or allow **selected virtual networks and IP ranges**; use a **private endpoint** for private access. The **Allow trusted Microsoft services** exception lets named Azure services through the firewall. They still need permission to the data.")
C(2,"Rotation and expiry?","Set **expiration dates**. Keys support an **auto-rotation policy**. Certificates can **auto-renew** with an integrated CA. Secrets rotate with Event Grid 'near expiry' events and automation. Each object has **versions**.")
C(2,"Secrets scanning with Defender CSPM, and Defender for Key Vault?","**Defender CSPM agentless secrets scanning** finds plaintext secrets and keys on VMs and in cloud deployments, and shows them in recommendations and **attack paths**. **Defender for Key Vault** raises **alerts** on unusual or suspicious access to vaults.")
Q(2,"An app's managed identity must read secret values from one vault and nothing else. Which role should you assign?","Key Vault Secrets User",["Key Vault Administrator","Key Vault Reader","Key Vault Secrets Officer"],"Secrets User reads secret contents. Reader sees metadata only. Officer can also create and delete.")
Q(2,"You must make sure no one, including a subscription Owner, can permanently delete keys in a vault before 90 days pass. What should you enable?","Purge protection",["A ReadOnly resource lock","Vault access policies","Soft delete only"],"Purge protection blocks purging until the retention period ends and cannot be turned off.")
Q(2,"A storage account uses a customer-managed key. The vault firewall blocks public access. What lets the storage service reach the vault?","Allow trusted Microsoft services to bypass the firewall, plus key permissions for the storage identity",["A user-defined route to the vault","Turning off soft delete","Granting Key Vault Reader to all users"],"The trusted services exception covers network access. The service identity still needs data-plane permission.")
Q(2,"Which TWO statements about Key Vault soft delete are true?",["It cannot be disabled once on","The retention period cannot be changed after the vault is created"],["Its default retention is 14 days","It only protects certificates"],"Soft delete is permanent, 7 to 90 days (default 90), fixed at creation, and covers vaults, keys, secrets and certificates.")
YN(2,["Key Vault Reader can read the value of a secret.","Premium tier is needed for HSM-protected keys.","A user with Contributor on the vault can read secrets when the vault uses Azure RBAC, without any data-plane role."],[0,1,0],"Reader sees metadata. Premium adds HSM keys. With RBAC, data access needs a data-plane role.")
M(2,"Match each task to the least-privileged Key Vault role.",[("Read a secret value","Key Vault Secrets User"),("Create and delete secrets","Key Vault Secrets Officer"),("Encrypt and decrypt with a key","Key Vault Crypto User"),("Permanently delete a soft-deleted vault","Key Vault Purge Operator")],"User roles use objects. Officer roles manage them.")
Q(2,"Defender for Cloud shows an attack path where an internet-exposed VM holds a plaintext storage key. Which capability found the key?","Agentless secrets scanning in Defender CSPM",["Defender for Key Vault alerts","Key Vault diagnostic logs","Azure Policy Audit effect"],"Agentless secrets scanning inspects machine disks for secrets and feeds attack path analysis.")
Q(2,"You need an alert when a vault is accessed from a Tor exit node. What should you enable?","Defender for Key Vault",["Purge protection","A private endpoint","Key auto-rotation"],"Defender for Key Vault detects unusual and suspicious access patterns.")
D(2,"Soft delete","Purge protection","Off by default and can never be disabled once on.",1,"Soft delete is on by default. Purge protection is optional and irreversible.")
D(2,"Key Vault Secrets User","Key Vault Reader","Can read the secret's value.",0,"Reader only sees properties.")
D(2,"Azure RBAC","Vault access policy","Recommended model that can scope access to a single secret.",0,"RBAC supports object-level scope.")
D(2,"Defender CSPM","Defender for Key Vault","Finds plaintext secrets left on VM disks.",0,"CSPM scans for exposed secrets. Defender for Key Vault alerts on vault access.")
# ---- 3 Governance and regulatory compliance
C(3,"Built-in vs custom policy definitions?","**Built-in:** maintained by Microsoft (allowed locations, require HTTPS…). **Custom:** your own JSON rule with `if` and `then.effect`. Group either into an **initiative** and **assign** at management group, subscription or resource group, with exclusions and **exemptions**.")
C(3,"Security standards in Defender for Cloud?","The **Microsoft cloud security benchmark (MCSB)** is assigned by default and drives **recommendations** and **secure score**. Add **regulatory standards** (ISO 27001, PCI DSS, NIST…) and custom standards. Standards are built on **Azure Policy** initiatives.")
C(3,"Regulatory compliance dashboard?","Shows each standard's controls as passed or failed, based on the assessed resources. Adding standards beyond the default needs a **paid Defender plan**. You can download reports and Microsoft's audit attestations.")
C(3,"Managing recommendations?","**Remediate** (often a Fix button), **exempt** a resource (waived or mitigated), **disable** a rule, or assign an **owner and due date** with governance rules. **Deny** and **Enforce** options stop new non-compliant resources.")
C(3,"Custom Azure role: the parts?","**Actions** and **NotActions** (management plane), **DataActions** and **NotDataActions** (data plane), and **AssignableScopes** (where it can be assigned). NotActions subtracts from Actions; it is **not** a deny.")
C(3,"Custom Microsoft Entra roles?","Built from Entra permissions (for example app registration management) and assigned tenant-wide or scoped to an object or administrative unit. They need **Microsoft Entra ID P1**.")
C(3,"Finding and fixing overprivileged access?","Use **Access control (IAM)** to review assignments at each scope, **PIM** to make standing roles eligible, **access reviews** to recertify, and swap broad roles (Owner, Contributor) for narrow or custom ones. Prefer **groups** over direct user assignments.")
C(3,"Azure Backup security features?","**Soft delete** (14 days default, up to 180, always-on option), **immutable vault** (blocks operations that would lose recovery points; can be **locked**), and **multi-user authorization** with a **Resource Guard** owned by a different admin.")
C(3,"Security controls with infrastructure as code?","Define controls in **Bicep, ARM templates or Terraform** (policy assignments, role assignments, locks, Defender plans) so every environment gets the same baseline. Add **what-if** and template scanning in the pipeline before deployment.")
Q(3,"A backup admin's account is compromised. You need a second person, in another team, to approve disabling soft delete or reducing retention on the vault. What should you configure?","Multi-user authorization with a Resource Guard",["A CanNotDelete lock","Vault redundancy set to GRS","A custom RBAC role with NotActions"],"A Resource Guard owned by someone else gates critical vault operations.")
Q(3,"You must show auditors how your subscriptions measure against PCI DSS. What should you do in Defender for Cloud?","Add the PCI DSS standard and review the regulatory compliance dashboard",["Raise the secure score to 100%","Enable just-in-time VM access","Create an Azure budget"],"The dashboard maps assessments to each standard's controls.")
Q(3,"A custom role lists Actions: Microsoft.Compute/* and NotActions: Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/delete. A user also has Contributor on the same scope. Can the user delete VMs?","Yes, because NotActions is not a deny and Contributor grants delete",["No, NotActions always blocks the action","No, custom roles override built-in roles","Only after activating PIM"],"NotActions only subtracts within that role. Another assignment can still grant the action.")
Q(3,"You need to stop anyone from deploying storage accounts that allow public blob access, across all subscriptions. What should you use?","An Azure Policy assignment with the Deny effect at the management group",["A resource lock on each subscription","A Defender for Storage alert","An access review"],"Deny blocks non-compliant deployments, and management group scope covers every subscription under it.")
Q(3,"Which TWO help reduce standing privileged access?",["Convert active role assignments to eligible in PIM","Run access reviews on privileged roles"],["Assign Owner at the root management group","Share one admin account between the team"],"PIM removes standing access. Reviews remove what is no longer needed.")
YN(3,["The Microsoft cloud security benchmark is assigned by default in Defender for Cloud.","A locked immutable vault's immutability setting can be turned off later.","Custom Microsoft Entra roles require Entra ID P1."],[1,0,1],"MCSB is the default standard. Locking immutability is irreversible. Custom Entra roles need P1.")
M(3,"Match each requirement to the control.",[("Block resources outside approved regions","Azure Policy Deny"),("Protect recovery points from deletion","Immutable vault"),("Stop accidental deletion of a resource group","Resource lock"),("Same security baseline in every environment","Infrastructure as code")],"Policy shapes, vaults keep, locks protect, IaC repeats.")
Q(3,"A team needs to restart VMs and read their metrics, nothing more. No built-in role fits. What should you create?","A custom Azure role with only those Actions and the needed AssignableScopes",["A custom Entra role","A new management group","A policy initiative"],"Custom Azure roles grant exactly the management-plane actions you list.")
D(3,"Azure Policy","Resource lock","Evaluates resource properties and reports compliance.",0,"Policy evaluates. Locks only block change or delete.")
D(3,"NotActions","Deny assignment","Truly blocks an action even if another role grants it.",1,"NotActions just subtracts inside one role.")
D(3,"Secure score","Regulatory compliance","Shows pass or fail per control of ISO 27001.",1,"Compliance maps to standards. Secure score measures overall posture.")
D(3,"Soft delete (Backup)","Multi-user authorization","Needs approval from the owner of a Resource Guard.",1,"MUA adds a second approver.")
# ---- 4 Storage accounts
C(4,"Baseline hardening for a storage account?","**Require secure transfer** (HTTPS), **minimum TLS 1.2**, **disallow anonymous blob access**, **disallow Shared Key** access (forces Microsoft Entra authorization), restrict **network access**, and limit **SAS** lifetime with a SAS expiration policy.")
C(4,"Why disable Shared Key authorization?","Account keys give **full access** and cannot be tied to a person. Disabling Shared Key means requests must use **Microsoft Entra ID** (RBAC data roles), which also blocks **account and service SAS**. User delegation SAS still works.")
C(4,"Storage firewall rules?","Set public network access to **selected networks**: **virtual network rules** (need a service endpoint), **IP rules** (public ranges only), **resource instance rules**, and the **trusted Microsoft services** exception. Or disable public access and use **private endpoints**.")
C(4,"Encryption options for storage?","Always encrypted at rest (AES-256). Choose **Microsoft-managed keys** or **customer-managed keys** in Key Vault/Managed HSM. **Infrastructure encryption** double-encrypts (set at creation). **Encryption scopes** give containers or blobs their own key.")
C(4,"Data roles for blob access with Entra ID?","**Storage Blob Data Reader**, **Contributor** and **Owner** (Owner also sets POSIX ACLs and ownership). Management roles such as Contributor do **not** grant blob data access by themselves.")
C(4,"Stored access policies?","Defined on a container, share, queue or table. A **service SAS** can point at one for its start, expiry and permissions. **Change or delete the policy to revoke** every SAS that uses it. Maximum **five** per container.")
C(4,"Defender for Storage: what does it do?","**Activity monitoring** (alerts on unusual access, exfiltration, suspicious IPs; no resource logs needed), **malware scanning** (**on-upload** and **on-demand**, Microsoft Defender Antivirus, priced per GB) and **sensitive data threat detection** (no extra cost).")
C(4,"Malware scanning settings?","A **monthly cap** on GB scanned per account, results as **blob index tags**, to **Event Grid** (automation) or **Log Analytics** (audit), and optional **soft delete of malicious blobs**. Hash reputation analysis is a lighter check that does not read the whole file.")
Q(4,"All access to a storage account must be authorized with Microsoft Entra ID so that every request maps to an identity. What should you configure?","Disallow Shared Key authorization",["Regenerate both access keys monthly","Enable hierarchical namespace","Set the default tier to Cool"],"With Shared Key off, account keys and key-signed SAS stop working, leaving Entra authorization.")
Q(4,"A web app lets customers upload files to Blob Storage. Files must be checked for malware as they arrive, and bad ones handled automatically. What should you enable?","Defender for Storage on-upload malware scanning with results sent to Event Grid",["Blob versioning","A lifecycle management rule","Hash-based soft delete"],"On-upload scanning checks each blob, and Event Grid lets a function or logic app quarantine it.")
Q(4,"A user with the Contributor role on a storage account gets 403 when listing blobs with Entra authorization in the portal. Why?","Contributor is a management role; a Storage Blob Data role is needed",["The account uses ZRS","Blob soft delete is on","The user needs the Reader role as well"],"Data-plane access needs a data role such as Storage Blob Data Reader.")
Q(4,"Which TWO settings reduce the risk of data being read anonymously or over an insecure channel?",["Disallow anonymous blob access","Require secure transfer"],["Enable large file shares","Enable change feed"],"One blocks public containers, the other forces HTTPS.")
YN(4,["Defender for Storage activity monitoring needs diagnostic resource logs to be enabled first.","A stored access policy can revoke the service SAS tokens that reference it.","IP network rules can allow a private address range such as 10.0.0.0/24."],[0,1,0],"Activity monitoring needs no resource logs. Policies revoke linked SAS. IP rules take public ranges only.")
M(4,"Match each goal to the storage feature.",[("Detect a malicious file as it is uploaded","On-upload malware scanning"),("Use your own key in Key Vault","Customer-managed keys"),("Reach the account on a private IP","Private endpoint"),("Revoke a set of SAS tokens at once","Stored access policy")],"Detect, encrypt, isolate, revoke.")
Q(4,"You need to keep malware scanning costs predictable on a high-traffic account. What should you set?","A monthly cap on GB scanned",["A SAS expiration policy","The access tier to Archive","Infrastructure encryption"],"The cap stops scanning for the month when reached, and alerts warn at 75% and 100%.")
Q(4,"Different containers in one account must be encrypted with different keys. What should you use?","Encryption scopes",["Separate access keys","Stored access policies","Blob index tags"],"An encryption scope assigns its own key to a container or blob.")
D(4,"Malware scanning","Hash reputation analysis","Reads the full content of the file with Defender Antivirus.",0,"Hash reputation only compares hashes.")
D(4,"Storage Blob Data Reader","Reader","Can read the contents of blobs.",0,"Reader is management-plane only.")
D(4,"Service endpoint","Private endpoint","Gives the account a private IP in your VNet.",1,"Service endpoints keep the public IP.")
D(4,"Shared Key","Microsoft Entra authorization","Ties each request to a user or managed identity.",1,"Keys are anonymous to the audit trail.")
